  "title": "Battle of Isandlwana",
  "summary": "On 22 January 1879, in the opening encounter of the Anglo-Zulu War, a Zulu army under King Cetshwayo overran the British camp at the foot of Isandlwana hill after Lord Chelmsford split his column. About 1,700 men were in the camp and only some 60 white and 400 black survivors are recorded. Britain won the war in July 1879.",
